{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "title": "Warehouse \u2014 Inventory & Storage",
  "uid": "warehouse-inventory-storage",
  "tags": [
    "warehouse",
    "inventory-storage",
    "bounded-context"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "30s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "API Gateway (Kong) \u2014 north-south view of this context's route",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request rate (Kong)",
      "description": "Requests/sec Kong forwarded to this context's Service, by HTTP status code. Kong sees a request even when the upstream pod never got instrumented (e.g. crashed before otelchi ran).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (code) (rate(kong_http_requests_total{service=~\"httproute\\.warehouse-systems\\.inventory-storage\\..*\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{code}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Error rate (Kong, 5xx)",
      "description": "5xx responses Kong returned or proxied for this context, as a fraction of all requests. A 5xx here with a flat upstream error rate on the service's own panel below means Kong itself (or the network to the upstream) is failing, not the application.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(kong_http_requests_total{service=~\"httproute\\.warehouse-systems\\.inventory-storage\\..*\", code=~\"5..\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(kong_http_requests_total{service=~\"httproute\\.warehouse-systems\\.inventory-storage\\..*\"}[5m])), 1e-9)",
          "legendFormat": "5xx ratio"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency p95 (Kong request vs. upstream)",
      "description": "kong_request_latency_ms is the full time Kong spent on the request (queueing + upstream + Kong overhead); kong_upstream_latency_ms isolates just the time waiting on this context's pod. A gap between the two that grows means Kong itself, not the service, is the bottleneck.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(kong_request_latency_ms_bucket{service=~\"httproute\\.warehouse-systems\\.inventory-storage\\..*\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "request (Kong total) p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(kong_upstream_latency_ms_bucket{service=~\"httproute\\.warehouse-systems\\.inventory-storage\\..*\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "upstream (service) p95"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Service HTTP RED (OLTP + projector + reports + MCP)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request rate by route",
      "description": "http_server_request_duration_seconds_count, the otelchi RED metric every fleet service emits per ADR-0009. Filtered to service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\" so the OLTP, analytics projector/reports and MCP processes all show up on one panel.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (service_name, http_route) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}} {{http_route}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Error rate (HTTP 5xx, by process)",
      "description": "5xx responses this context's own processes returned, split by which process (OLTP vs. reports vs. MCP) so a reports-only outage doesn't get hidden inside a healthy OLTP average. Two label variants are unioned: newer otelchi/semconv releases in this fleet use http_response_status_code, older ones (riandyrn/otelchi metric package pre-dating the semconv bump) use http_status_code.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 10
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (service_name) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\", http_response_status_code=~\"5..\"}[5m])) or sum by (service_name) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\", http_status_code=~\"5..\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request duration p95, by process",
      "description": "http.server.request.duration histogram (seconds), the ONLY sanctioned RED-latency source per ADR-0009 -- no service hand-rolls its own HTTP timer.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 10
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (service_name, le) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}} p95"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Inventory & Storage \u2014 business metrics (Tier 2, ADR-0009)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "inventory_reservations_total",
      "description": "Reservations against usable inventory, by outcome (created or revoked). A revoke rate climbing towards the create rate means physical delivery is failing.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(inventory_reservations_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Go runtime (this context's processes)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Goroutines",
      "description": "go.goroutine.count for service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\". A steady climb with no matching traffic growth is a goroutine leak.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "go_goroutine_count{service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\"} or runtime_go_goroutines{service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Go memory used",
      "description": "go.memory.used for service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\".",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 28
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "go_memory_used_bytes{service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\"} or runtime_go_mem_heap_alloc_bytes{service_name=~\"inventory-(storage|projector|reports).*\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}} {{go_memory_type}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Logs (this context's pods, application containers only)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Live log stream",
      "description": "Raw JSON log lines from every Inventory & Storage pod (OLTP + frontend + mcp + projector + reports), excluding the istio-proxy/istio-init sidecar containers. Every fleet service writes structured JSON via log/slog with the active trace_id/span_id already embedded (telemetry.WithTraceContext) -- click a line's \"trace_id\" field to pivot into the matching Jaeger trace via the Loki datasource's derived-fields link (observability.tf).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "{app=\"inventory-storage\", container!~\"istio-proxy|istio-init\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{pod}} / {{container}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "showLabels": true,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": false,
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Log volume by level",
      "description": "Lines per second, split by the `level` label Alloy lifts out of each JSON body's `level` field (logging.tf's stage.json/stage.labels) -- a real Loki label, not a per-line regex, so this is cheap even at high volume. A WARN/ERROR line here with no corresponding change on the HTTP RED error-rate panel above is worth investigating: it means something is going wrong that never surfaces as a failed request (a background consumer, a retried publish, a degraded fallback).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 37
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (level) (count_over_time({app=\"inventory-storage\", container!~\"istio-proxy|istio-init\"}[$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{level}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Errors and warnings only",
      "description": "Same stream as \"Live log stream\", filtered to level=~\"ERROR|WARN\" so a real problem does not scroll off the bottom of a busy INFO-heavy pod.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 46
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "{app=\"inventory-storage\", container!~\"istio-proxy|istio-init\", level=~\"ERROR|WARN\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{pod}} / {{container}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "showLabels": true,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": false,
